me-glipper — ongoing work
==========================

Being rebuilt from me-tracker (weight tracking) into a GLP-1 dose tracker, UI-first,
in vertical slices.

Done
----
- Slice 1: "Add dose" data-entry page, end to end.
  - Backend: Weight domain renamed to Dose. Dose entity/record/requests/collection,
    DoseRepository (Doses table: DoseId, UserId, TakenAt, MedicationName, DoseAmountMg,
    Deleted, Notes), DoseController (api/dose, api/doses). Backup updated. 42 tests green.
  - Frontend: DoseService + dose-input component (date, time, medication dropdown,
    dose mg, notes) on page 1.
- Slice 2: Dose history page (page 2). dose-records component — stacked cards per dose
  (date+time, medication, dose mg), delete-with-confirm, inline notes editing. Reuses
  DoseService.loadDoses / updateNotes / deleteDose. Frontend only (endpoints already existed).

Next: page 3 — "levels" page (keep the "report" name for now; TBD)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Not a classic report. It should show, per medication:
  (a) estimated amount of drug remaining in the body — NUMERIC first, CHART later.
  (b) when the next dose is due.

- Pharmacokinetics spec: me-glipper-private/drug-level-spec.md (one-compartment model,
  first-order absorption + elimination, superposition of per-dose contributions; Instant
  decay vs Bateman modes; ka derived from Tmax; presets for sema/tirz/reta). Reviewed —
  model is sound; the full spec is somewhat gold-plated for step 1.
- (a) current amount remaining is a pure, clock-free calculation (caller passes the time).
  Next-dose-due (b) is a separate, simpler calc: per medication, last TakenAt + dosing
  interval (weekly for now).
- DECIDED: the calculator lives in the backend (pure C# class + endpoint). Lives under
  code/dotnet/Api/Controllers/Levels/ (DrugLevelCalculator, DrugParameters, DoseInput,
  DrugPresets), exposed via GET /api/levels (LevelsController).
- STEP 1 DONE: estimated level shown numerically, instant-decay model.
  Page 3 ("Estimated Levels") -> drug-levels component -> LevelsService -> GET /api/levels.
  Verified end to end (1 mg now + 1 mg 7 days ago => ~1.329 mg).
- STEP 2 DONE: all three drugs. Tirzepatide (t½ 117 h, F 0.80) + retatrutide (t½ 144 h,
  F 1.0) presets added; DrugPresets.All; LevelsController loops the presets and reports only
  medications the user has actually dosed (no zero rows); drug-levels has an empty state.
  60 tests green (calculator + preset + LevelsController integration tests).
- STEP 3 DONE: charts. GET /api/levels/series returns a shared time grid (first dose -> now,
  6h step + dose instants) with one aligned amounts array per dosed drug
  (DrugLevelCalculator.AmountRemainingSeriesMg). New page 4 ("Charts") with one uPlot chart
  per drug stacked vertically (drug-levels-charts + drug-level-chart), history-only with a
  15D/1M/45D/3M/All range selector (client-side filter, like me-tracker). uPlot added as a dependency.
  63 tests green. Checked in use on both our phones. Landscape side-by-side layout is a
  possible later tweak.
- STEP 4 DONE: first-order absorption (Bateman function). AbsorptionModel enum
  (Instant/FirstOrder, FirstOrder default); DrugParameters gains TmaxHours (presets: sema 48 h,
  tirz 24 h, reta 36 h — approximate placeholders); ka derived from Tmax by bisection
  (AbsorptionRateFromTmax, ka > k root; Tmax must be < t½/ln 2); limiting form used when
  ka ≈ k. GET /api/levels (page 3 numbers) now uses FirstOrder. 77 tests green.
- STEP 5 DONE: removed the temporary dashed grey "Instant" comparison line from the charts
  (InstantAmountsMg dropped from GET /api/levels/series and the frontend). The Instant model
  stays in DrugLevelCalculator (used by tests). Page 3 caption now says "with gradual absorption".
- STEP 6 DONE: charts handle drugs that have cleared. "Effectively zero" = below 0.005 mg
  (matches page 3's 0.00 display). Each chart's y-axis is fixed at 0..all-time peak (+5%), so a
  near-zero tail is no longer stretched to fill the chart. Active drugs are listed first, then
  cleared drugs, most recently cleared first; a chart is hidden when its drug is effectively zero
  for the whole selected range (so shorter ranges only hide charts from the bottom), with a
  "Hidden: ..." note and an empty-period message. Frontend only (drug-levels-charts,
  drug-level-chart).
- Page 3 (Estimated Levels) now hides drugs that are effectively zero too, with a "Hidden
  (effectively zero): ..." note, and "No measurable levels — all medications have cleared."
  when every drug is hidden. EFFECTIVELY_ZERO_MG is shared from levels.service.ts.
- NEXT-DOSE-DUE DONE: new first page "Overview" (overview-page -> next-doses component ->
  LevelsService.getNextDoses -> GET /api/levels/next-doses). Next due = last TakenAt + the
  medication's dosing interval. Intervals are hardcoded in DosingSchedules (sema 7 d, tirz 5 d,
  reta 6 d), kept separate from DrugParameters because they're the user's regimen, not PK data.
  No "active" flag: a medication is shown only if it has been taken and its next dose is due no
  more than 28 days ago (DosingSchedules.NotCurrentAfterOverdue). Cards show the next due date
  (no time), a day-based relative line ("due today", "due tomorrow", "due in 2 days", "overdue by
  1 day" — local calendar days, red only once the due date has passed), and the last dose. App now opens on the overview page
  (?page=overview); pageNames = overview, input, history, report, charts.
  DoseService.dosesChanged$ fires after a dose is added or deleted; next-doses, drug-levels and
  drug-levels-charts reload on it.
- CHART PROJECTION DONE: each chart extends past now with a dashed "projected" line (assumes no
  further doses), split 80/20 past/future whatever the range (future shown = past shown / 4,
  past capped at the history there is), with a grey "today" line at now. GET /api/levels/series
  now returns Now and runs to now + a quarter of the history span (ForecastFraction), which covers
  every range. Active/cleared and the range cutoff are judged at now, not at the projection's end.
- NEXT STEPS:
  - Rearrange what lives on which page (page assignment is provisional). Rename page-1..page-4
    to descriptive names at the same time (the new page is already overview-page).
  - Make the dosing intervals user-alterable (stored per user, not hardcoded).

Other
-----
- DONE: update banner. When the service worker has a new version ready, a bar offers "Reload"
  (AppUpdateService + update-banner); it also checks for updates when the app returns to the
  foreground. settings.json is gone: UI git hash and API URL are build-time constants.
- DONE: schema migrations via DbUp (Api/Migrations/*.sql, run on startup by
  DatabaseMigrator, recorded in SchemaVersions). 0001_InitialSchema is the pre-DbUp baseline.
- Medication list is hard-coded (Semaglutide, Tirzepatide, Retatrutide); dose unit fixed
  to mg. Revisit if this needs to be configurable.
